that creates every alt group might have a bigger list.

Betsy

PS *my* practice on alt group creation (unofficial, not a formal policy,
posted every semester to the users with invitation to comment.)

1) any group that I am interested in
2) any group that I guess someone at my site will be interested in
   eg alt.sex.stories.hetero or alt.internet.media-coverage
3) any group that starts getting a lot of traffic 
4) any group that anyone at my site requests (anonymous notes under
   the door are ok) 
5) all messages from jfurr and other frequent alt posters, or from the 
   occasional newbie who starts flooding the net with newgroups or
   rmgroups, and all messages with "scientology" or "paulina" in them
   and all badly formed and unapproved messages are deleted, unread.
   (if the world wants the group, we start getting traffic)
 
We turn the expire on all binaries sub-hierarchies all the way up so that
the stuff doesn't overflow the disk. We keep ne.* and news.* for a month,
comp for a week, talk.* for two days, binaries for a day or less, and
everything else for three or four days. We tinker a bit with expiration
times using roughly the same criteria as for alt groups. I'll keep any
group except binaries groups for a week if requested.  I don't have any
auto-tuning yet and I spend about three less-than-5-minute sessions a week
adding and removing groups.


 

